WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.834
-Hey!

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.334
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:07.400
-Hey!

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.000
Hey!

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
♪♪

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.334
-Whoo-hoo!

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:16.400
♪♪

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.267
-[ Chuckles ]
-Okay.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.534
Can you just make yourself
visible, already?

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.033
[ Whoosh ]

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.667
-What?
Why didn't he do that sooner?

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.133
-I don't know.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.100
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with David Harbour.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:30.934
That was a clip
from "We Have a Ghost."

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:35.367
Now, I think it's very clear
from that clip you play a ghost.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.834
Usually, when we show a clip

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:38.667
from one of the stars
of a film who's here,

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.734
we make sure that clip
has lines from them,

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.834
but you don't have a single line
in this movie.

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:46.367
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:50.133
I have some --
I improvised some moans.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.100
-Yeah? Oh, they let you
do a few moans?

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.634
-[ Moans ]
-Oh, very good.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.267
-Thank you.
-Very well cast.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:57.634
-Yeah, no lie.
They sent me the script.

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:02.100
And it was, you know, "You are
one of the leads of this movie,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.601
walking around, doing things,
being a ghost,

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.367
and you have no lines."
-Yeah.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:12.701
-And I was like, "Yes!
-I mean, so, so nice, right?

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.367
-Easy gig.
-Yeah.

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:17.834
-And it's a great cast.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.801
Anthony Mackie.
-Who's wonderful.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:23.067
-He's great. I love him.
Also this younger actor,

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:25.667
Jahi Winston, who I think
is really special.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.968
Like, really soulful kid.
I really liked him.

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.300
-That's really cool

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.968
to work with people like that
you never met before.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.334
You also worked
with Jennifer Coolidge.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.701
-Yes, Jennifer Coolidge, yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:40.000
And she is as amazing
as you think she would be.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.634
-Yeah. In person, she's
everything you want her to be.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.734
-Yeah.
-It's really great.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.601
-It's just what you see
on a talk show

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.601
or at an awards show.
It just is that.

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.467
And it's not that way
with some of us.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:50.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:54.734
But, the -- yeah.
She was incredible.

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.067
She's so funny.
There's one scene --

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.767
I don't think
I'm spoiling the film.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:02.634
It's not like Marvel here.
But there is a scene in the film

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:05.501
where I frighten her.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:09.601
And she runs screaming
and jumps out a window.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.033
And you think, like,
in the script,

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.400
it just says, like, "Runs
screaming out the window."

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.067
I swear, there were like --
we did about 15 takes.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.534
And every take, she was like,
"Let's try it again."

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:21.634
[ Laughter ]
"Maybe I could go like this.

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:23.534
'Ooh, ooh, ooh!'"

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:28.734
It's like I've never seen any --
every animal, every sound was --

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.801
it was a lesson.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.167
-It was an acting class.
-If there's any actor

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:35.534
who thought through 15 ways
to jump out a window,

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.701
I'm happy it's her.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:40.334
-She also had this amazing --
We have this amazing moment

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:43.200
where there's a CGI thing
that shoots out of my face,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.200
and it's a hand
and it strangles her.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.834
And you know,
so I did it with my hand.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.434
I just, like -- and
she was, like, really pissed.

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:51.834
We stopped the take.
And she was like,

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:54.534
"David, you got to
really strangle me.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:56.968
You got to strangle me!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.267
I was like, "Jen, you're --
You know, what do you --

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:02.000
I'm not gonna murder
America's sweetheart."

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:06.434
She's like, "Come on! Come on!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:08.367
-Well, I'm glad
you didn't murder her.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.200
I'm glad you trusted
your own instincts.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.667
-Yeah.
-One last thing

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:14.667
I want to ask you.
No details, no spoilers.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.801
But I know you're about
to embark on the final --

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.767
you're filming your last
of "Stranger Things".

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.467
-Yeah.
-What an incredible journey

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.734
it must be to watch
not just this show take off

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:25.634
but also to watch
all those kids grow up.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:27.834
-Yeah, yeah.
It'll be really special.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:30.934
We go back in, I think,
May or June.

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.000
And we shoot the final season.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.968
And you know, it's been,
at this point, eight years.

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:39.501
It'll be 10 years of my life
by the time that wraps.

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:42.834
And so -- And you know, it did
everything for me, that show.

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:45.467
It created a whole new career
for me.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.434
-And we've all been
the beneficiaries of it.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:49.334
It's been so cool how many
people in that show

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.934
we didn't know before
that we got to see

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.767
for the first time and
then see everywhere else.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.467
Man, it is just always
such a pleasure

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.734
to have you here.
Thank you so much, David.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.300
-Thanks.
-David Harbour!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:00.968
-"We Have a Ghost" premieres
February 24th on Netflix.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:02.634
We'll be right back
with Kathryn Newton.

